  "designNotes": [
    "Exploratory integration of scoped accepted components; no full-stage approval.",
    "Four clawed digits per paw copy the illustration, not a new species fact.",
    "Smooth ear tissue and body volume only; shaggy hair and coat are deferred.",
    "Tail proportions approximate study-0018; continuous geometry is a new candidate.",
    "Revision 2 closes the neck-to-chest gap and rounds the shoulder and pelvis sweep caps; no paired rear masses.",
    "Revision 3 replaces capped torso with rounded volumes, buries proximal thigh ends, reduces ocular protrusion and reports bounded voxel-debris cleanup.",
    "Revision 4 removes overlapping chest bands with a continuous torso sweep and increases elevated-camera framing only. Six principal cameras retain identical scale.",
    "Nick requested modestly stronger-looking hind legs inspired by rabbit bounding power, explicitly not literal rabbit legs. Revision 5 increases thigh and calf volume while preserving limb paths, lengths, joint positions, stance, paws, pelvis, tail, head and cameras.",
    "Nick found the fuller legs somewhat improved but the shin too wavy. Revision 6 places the intermediate lower-leg controls on the knee-to-ankle line while retaining thigh and calf radii, knee and ankle endpoints, feet and all other body parameters. Smooth transitions remain local to the joints; no literal rabbit anatomy.",
    "Revision 7 resolves ankle and wrist connections at construction level. Keep the straight shin and fuller leg volume. Local ankle contour leads into a short sloped foot bridge; remove the low rear pad extension and rounded forepaw ball. A tapered carpal transition opens into a compact paw mass. Existing toes, claws, limb stance, head, torso and tail remain unchanged. New joint forms are provisional visual interpretations of paw study-0020, not ratified skeletal facts."
  ],
